[h1]v0.2.0 - Drivetrain feel[/h1]

[h2]What you need to do[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]ZombieBuddy users:[/b] nothing, Steam updates the mod and the new features come with it.
[*][b]Manual install:[/b] copy the zombie folder from B42.21_Manual_Install over your old one again (the vehicle controller changed).
[*][b]Dedicated servers:[/b] nothing, servers still need no Java install.
[/list]

[h2]What is new[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Engine braking.[/b] Lift off the throttle in gear and the engine now slows the car; the revs follow your road speed, and a downshift raises them. There is a strength slider (0 turns it off) and an optional lock-up for a gear far too low. It never takes more than half your tyre grip.
[*][b]Manual clutch, neutral and stalling[/b] (both opt-in, for manual shifting). Hold the clutch key (Left Ctrl by default) to disengage, pick neutral between reverse and first, and stall the engine if you let the clutch out in too high a gear with no throttle.
[*][b]On-screen stick shift.[/b] An H-pattern gate on the HUD shows R, N and the gears; the knob moves as you shift, goes amber with the clutch in and red when you stall.
[*][b]Engine-type shift points[/b] (opt-in). The automatic gearbox shifts like the vehicle's engine type: vans early, sports cars late.
[*]The vehicle info panel says which Java part is running (ZombieBuddy, manual install or missing).
[*][b]New languages:[/b] Chinese (Simplified), Portuguese (Brazil), Spanish, German, Turkish and French. These are machine translated first drafts, so please tell me what reads wrong.
[*]The "Reference power and weight" tooltip now explains that it applies to every car and that the power number shown is the game's engine force, not horsepower.
[/list]

Engine braking is the only new effect that is on by default, at a moderate strength. If you do not like it, set Engine braking to 0 in the Drivetrain page of the sandbox options and the car coasts like before.
